Definition — Array <p>A collection of elements of the same type, stored in a contiguous block of memory, accessed by an integer index (0-based in C, C++, Java, Python).</p> <pre><code>int a[5] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
// a[0]=10, a[1]=20, a[2]=30, a[3]=40, a[4]=50
</code></pre>   Key properties:  - **Homogeneous** — all elements same type. - **Contiguous** — one block of memory. - **Fixed size** (in statically typed languages). - **Indexed** — 0-based.
